
* Write a Java program using `ClassLoadingMXBean` to print the number of currently loaded, total loaded, and unloaded classes.
* Write a Java program using `ManagementFactory.getMemoryPoolMXBeans()` to identify the Metaspace memory pool when available.
* Write a Java program that periodically reports Metaspace usage, committed memory, and maximum memory.
* Write a Java program that compares heap usage and Metaspace usage using JVM management APIs.
* Write a Java program that loads a class dynamically using `Class.forName()` and explains what happens during class loading.
* Write a Java program that demonstrates class initialization using static fields and static initialization blocks.
* Write a Java program that loads the same class name through two different custom class loaders and demonstrates that the resulting classes are distinct JVM types.
* Write a Java program that creates a custom class loader and loads a class from a class file.
* Write a Java program that creates a custom class loader and demonstrates the conditions required for it to become eligible for garbage collection.
* Write a Java program that retains a custom class loader in a static collection and explain how this can prevent class unloading.
* Modify the preceding program to remove the retained class-loader reference and investigate class unloading using JVM diagnostics.
